  "trend_method": "Mean temperature, mean daily maximum temperature, and mean daily minimum temperature use ordinary least-squares linear trends with lag-1 HAC/Newey-West uncertainty. Other temperature indicators use Sen's slope to estimate trend magnitude and the Mann-Kendall test to assess statistical significance. For Sen/Mann-Kendall analyses, the Hamed-Rao variance correction is applied only when significant serial correlation is detected after detrending. Statistical significance is assessed at p < 0.05. For Yukon maps, Benjamini-Hochberg false-discovery-rate correction is applied across grid cells. Community heatmaps use the same multiple-testing control across communities.",
  "community_multiple_testing": "Community significance is additionally reported using Benjamini-Hochberg FDR correction within each indicator.",
